A pre-v6 entry no longer vanishes when the vault moves to per-entry records. Its record ends in an empty data-key field, which the parser stripped and then rejected, so after an `add` the older entry left `list`, `unseal` and `check`, and `check` still called the vault consistent. A record that opens but holds no entry line is now counted: `check` reports it and fails, and `unseal` refuses to restore part of the vault.
